$DIR/test.p:34:17: cannot assign to v[0].x: v[0] is a copy returned by the Index method of *PV
    x[k] on a container is a copy that its Index method returns, so assigning to
    a field or element of it would change only the copy. This is the same rule
    as Go's for map elements.
    Read the element, change it, and store it back with x[k] = v, or change it
    in place through a pointer from a method such as Ptr.
    Store the changed element back:
        p := v[i]
        p.x = 1
        v[i] = p
    (see "Indexing library containers" in the Plutonium spec, section 11.11)
    (run "pluto explain E2455" for a longer explanation)
